    "readme_description": "A permutation `perm` of `n + 1` integers of all the integers in the range `[0, n]` can be represented as a string `s` of length `n` where:\n\n- `s[i] == 'I'` if `perm[i] < perm[i + 1]`, and\n- `s[i] == 'D'` if `perm[i] > perm[i + 1]`.\n\nGiven a string `s`, reconstruct the permutation `perm` and return it. If there are multiple valid permutations `perm`, return **any of them**.",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: s = \"IDID\"\nOutput: [0,4,1,3,2]\nExplanation: [0,4,1,3,2] is one valid answer.\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: s = \"III\"\nOutput: [0,1,2,3]\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: s = \"DDI\"\nOutput: [3,2,0,1]\n```"
            }
        ]
    },
    "readme_constraints": "- `1 <= s.length <= 10^5`\n- `s[i]` is either `'I'` or `'D'`.",
